            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the evidence showing that apolipoprotein (apo) B and A-1 are superior to the conventional cholesterol indices as analytes in laboratory practice, indices of the lipoprotein-related risk for vascular disease, and measures of the adequacy of low-density lipoprotein-lowering therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
